# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your own values.
# `.env.local` is git-ignored. Never commit a real Client ID or a client secret.
#
# The Client ID comes from your Spotify app: https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard
# PKCE needs only the Client ID. There is no client secret in this app, by design.

VITE_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=

# Optional. Leave EMPTY unless you need an override.
#
# The app works out its redirect URI from the browser's own origin, so it cannot
# drift from where you actually run it: <origin>/callback, for example
#   http://127.0.0.1:5173/callback   (npm run dev)      <-- register this for local dev
#   https://your-site.example/callback                  (deployed)
# The exact same string is sent to /authorize and again on the token exchange.
#
# Register that exact URI on the Spotify app under Settings -> Redirect URIs.
# It is compared character for character: no trailing slash, and use
# `127.0.0.1` rather than `localhost`.
#
# Only set this if the app is served at a different URL from the one you browse
# to (e.g. a proxy or tunnel). If you set it and it does not match the address
# you opened, the browser lands on another origin, the PKCE verifier stored
# under the first origin is not found, and sign-in fails with "session expired".
# VITE_SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_URI=
